{%- comment -%}
  seo-brand-context.liquid - Wooffy brand reinforcement schema

  ==========================================================
  PASTE-INTO-SHOPIFY snippet. This file is in scripts/ for
  reference only; the live theme reads from snippets/ in the
  Shopify code editor.
  ==========================================================

  PURPOSE: Reinforce Google's recognition of "Wooffy" as the
  canonical brand identity for thewooffy.com. The existing
  Booster Apps SEO Organization schema correctly names the
  brand "Wooffy" but:
    1. Has no alternateName property (Google uses this for
       variant brand-string matching).
    2. The sameAs[] array contains empty strings from Shopify
       theme social-media settings where some platforms are
       configured with empty URLs (6 of 9 entries empty as of
       2026-06-21).

  This snippet emits a supplementary Organization JSON-LD
  using the same @id as the canonical Organization, which
  causes Google to MERGE the properties — adding alternateName,
  description, knowsAbout, and a clean sameAs[] containing only
  populated social profiles.

  ==========================================================
  HOW TO INSTALL (3 minutes in Shopify Admin)
  ==========================================================

  Step 1. Online Store → Themes → ⋯ (three dots) → Edit code

  Step 2. Left sidebar → Snippets folder → "Add a new snippet"
          → Name: seo-brand-context
          → Paste THE ENTIRE CONTENTS OF THIS FILE
            (the {% comment %} block is fine; Shopify strips it
            from output)
          → Save

  Step 3. Left sidebar → Layout → theme.liquid
          → Find the line: {{ content_for_header }}
          → Right AFTER that line, add a new line:
              {% render 'seo-brand-context' %}
          → If you already have {% render 'seo-article-freshness' %},
            put this new line right after it.
          → Save

  Step 4. Verify (1 minute): use https://search.google.com/test/rich-results
          → enter https://thewooffy.com/
          → confirm Organization schema shows alternateName +
            cleaned sameAs[] without empty strings

  Idempotent: emitting two JSON-LDs with the same @id is the
  correct schema.org pattern for property merging. Google
  handles this fine and treats it as a single Organization
  entity with the union of properties.
{%- endcomment -%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Organization",
  "@id": "{{ shop.url }}/#organization",
  "name": "Wooffy",
  "alternateName": ["Wooffy.com", "Wooffy Dog Breed Guides"],
  "url": "{{ shop.url }}",
  "logo": "{{ shop.url }}/cdn/shop/files/Logo_a50e828c-1066-4eec-8ff2-e41bdf8e6808.png",
  "description": "Wooffy publishes 700+ expert dog breed guides covering cost, care, grooming and nutrition for every dog — plus modern designer dog houses crafted for everyday comfort.",
  "knowsAbout": [
    "Dog breeds",
    "Dog nutrition",
    "Dog grooming",
    "Puppy care",
    "Dog health",
    "Modern dog houses"
  ],
  "sameAs": [
    "https://www.pinterest.com/wooffy_official/",
    "https://www.instagram.com/wooffy_official/",
    "https://www.youtube.com/@Wooffy_Official"
  ]
}
</script>
